1
00:00:16,013 --> 00:00:20,107
[Round 2 mission begins]
Welcome to Round 2 of X THE LEAGUE.

2
00:00:20,107 --> 00:00:24,788
Starting in Round 2,
sales alone won't decide the winner.

3
00:00:25,394 --> 00:00:28,440
Sales, strategy, and the fans' choice.

4
00:00:28,440 --> 00:00:32,044
The real competition begins,
and nothing can be overlooked.

5
00:00:32,044 --> 00:00:34,614
The Round 2 mission is...

6
00:00:34,614 --> 00:00:36,256
the Wild Card.

7
00:00:37,091 --> 00:00:40,473
[Wild Card?]

8
00:00:40,473 --> 00:00:44,123
A new seller will be brought in
to shake up the game.

9
00:00:46,208 --> 00:00:48,945
Countries will receive mission points

10
00:00:48,945 --> 00:00:55,150
in order of their new seller's sales,
from highest to lowest.

11
00:00:55,661 --> 00:00:58,670
[Round 2: Wild Card Start]

12
00:00:58,670 --> 00:01:01,225
[Korea]

13
00:01:01,225 --> 00:01:04,094
[Seoul, South Korea]

14
00:01:04,094 --> 00:01:06,721
[Who is Team Korea's Wild Card?]

15
00:01:14,044 --> 00:01:17,889
[Someone's getting an early-morning workout in]

16
00:01:23,618 --> 00:01:24,620
[Choi Seol Hwa, rising wellness star]

17
00:01:24,620 --> 00:01:27,361
Hello, I'm Choi Seol Hwa,

18
00:01:27,361 --> 00:01:31,103
Team Korea's Wild Card in X THE LEAGUE.

19
00:01:31,103 --> 00:01:33,108
Wellness is my specialty.

20
00:01:33,108 --> 00:01:37,175
Not many sellers are getting into wellness.

21
00:01:37,175 --> 00:01:38,593
It could be my advantage.

22
00:01:38,593 --> 00:01:40,642
[Choi Seol Hwa's strength: wellness specialist]

23
00:01:40,642 --> 00:01:41,808
For Team Korea,

24
00:01:41,808 --> 00:01:47,294
a team made up of K-fashion, beauty,
and tech-focused sellers,

25
00:01:47,294 --> 00:01:49,677
having a wellness specialist

26
00:01:49,677 --> 00:01:52,863
whose content is rooted in everyday life

27
00:01:52,863 --> 00:01:56,942
would mean adding another sales category.

28
00:01:56,942 --> 00:01:59,403
I'm expecting a big contribution from her.

29
00:02:00,084 --> 00:02:02,772
I started ballet in middle school
and did it for 10 years.

30
00:02:02,772 --> 00:02:06,887
I've been hitting the gym after I competed
in a bodybuilding competition.

31
00:02:06,887 --> 00:02:13,147
I work out to stay healthy
and share that with others.

32
00:02:13,147 --> 00:02:16,314
My personal training studio had to close down
because of COVID.

33
00:02:16,314 --> 00:02:19,587
[Hard times kept her
from doing what she loved]

34
00:02:19,587 --> 00:02:24,150
What I could do on my own was
model on Instagram.

35
00:02:24,150 --> 00:02:27,878
I looked at other ways to make a living.

36
00:02:27,878 --> 00:02:32,767
That's how I started as a seller.

37
00:02:32,767 --> 00:02:35,255
Workout equipment sells best.

38
00:02:35,255 --> 00:02:37,555
Workout equipment isn't something
you have to keep replacing.

39
00:02:37,555 --> 00:02:42,026
I can just leave the link up,
and it keeps selling.

40
00:02:42,026 --> 00:02:46,163
So I sell workout equipment,
I sell healthy foods,

41
00:02:46,163 --> 00:02:50,284
and I also host group buys
for wellness products.

42
00:02:50,835 --> 00:02:53,170
- I'll use it.
- No, it's mine.

43
00:02:53,170 --> 00:02:57,176
[Seller Choi Seol Hwa's other secret weapon]
- Stop using mine. - I need to look good, too.

44
00:02:57,176 --> 00:03:02,185
[Couple content featuring her husband]

45
00:03:02,185 --> 00:03:05,482
There's no acting in the couple content.

46
00:03:05,482 --> 00:03:07,585
We might talk about shooting it a certain way,

47
00:03:07,585 --> 00:03:10,264
but our personalities always come through.

48
00:03:10,264 --> 00:03:16,477
I think people respond well
because my husband and I have great chemistry.

49
00:03:16,477 --> 00:03:19,658
[Cheongju, Chungcheongbuk-do, South Korea]

50
00:03:19,658 --> 00:03:24,491
[Where are Seol Hwa and her husband?]
Here is our company profile and price list.

51
00:03:24,491 --> 00:03:28,194
We visited Nutricore's factory
in Chungcheongbuk-do today.

52
00:03:28,804 --> 00:03:32,376
I've been taking this product for a year now.

53
00:03:32,376 --> 00:03:34,845
I have to start selling now.

54
00:03:34,845 --> 00:03:38,860
I wanted to see if we could collaborate
on my next sale.

55
00:03:38,860 --> 00:03:40,778
That's why I visited them.

56
00:03:41,351 --> 00:03:46,141
I came here to pitch a collaboration.

57
00:03:46,141 --> 00:03:48,124
[Cutting to the chase]
I hope we can get a big discount.

58
00:03:48,124 --> 00:03:50,446
As you can tell from our price list,

59
00:03:50,446 --> 00:03:53,998
[A hard no]
our prices are on the higher end.

60
00:03:53,998 --> 00:03:57,039
I'll show you my account insights.

61
00:03:57,039 --> 00:04:00,589
This is my workout video,
and it gained me almost 3,000 followers.

62
00:04:00,589 --> 00:04:02,973
It's just a workout video.

63
00:04:02,973 --> 00:04:05,586
I also posted content

64
00:04:05,586 --> 00:04:09,691
where I genuinely talk about your products,
introducing them.

65
00:04:09,691 --> 00:04:12,608
I did an omega-3 deficiency test.

66
00:04:13,278 --> 00:04:16,884
Omega-3 deficiency is really common these days.

67
00:04:16,884 --> 00:04:18,907
Maybe 10%?

68
00:04:18,907 --> 00:04:20,564
[Did I hear that right?]
- Sorry? - 10%.

69
00:04:20,564 --> 00:04:22,213
[A smaller discount than expected]
- Ten. - Ten?

70
00:04:22,213 --> 00:04:28,872
I do carry them around in my bag
so I can take them with me.

71
00:04:28,872 --> 00:04:29,880
You do?

72
00:04:29,880 --> 00:04:34,476
I do.
Omega-3, probiotic supplements, and vitamin C.

73
00:04:34,476 --> 00:04:36,842
I take vitamin C twice a day.

74
00:04:36,842 --> 00:04:39,680
I would love to work with you
and host a group buy.

75
00:04:39,680 --> 00:04:43,873
I can see that you've done a lot of research
about our products.

76
00:04:43,873 --> 00:04:46,195
You've prepared a lot for this.

77
00:04:46,195 --> 00:04:47,296
I have.

78
00:04:47,296 --> 00:04:49,507
Can I get 23% off?

79
00:04:49,507 --> 00:04:53,357
Well, since you brought it up...

80
00:04:53,357 --> 00:04:55,842
I could give you a maximum of 19% off.

81
00:04:56,665 --> 00:04:58,920
That's already a pretty big discount for us.

82
00:04:58,920 --> 00:05:00,628
- Are you sure?
- Yes.

83
00:05:00,628 --> 00:05:03,148
Let's do 19%. I'll do my best.

84
00:05:03,148 --> 00:05:04,481
Thank you.

85
00:05:04,481 --> 00:05:07,814
I was going to make one more suggestion.

86
00:05:07,814 --> 00:05:12,576
Now that I'm here today,
I can post something right away.

87
00:05:12,576 --> 00:05:14,913
- I would like to do a giveaway.
- Okay.

88
00:05:14,913 --> 00:05:18,368
[A giveaway made possible with just a word]
It's insane I'm packaging this.

89
00:05:18,368 --> 00:05:20,593
Wow. What should I do?

90
00:05:20,593 --> 00:05:23,258
- Would you like to put them in the box?
- Sure.

91
00:05:24,288 --> 00:05:29,760
My followers are going to receive these,
so I need to package it carefully.

92
00:05:29,760 --> 00:05:31,729
I wanted to try packaging.

93
00:05:31,729 --> 00:05:34,398
I also wanted to turn it into content.

94
00:05:35,233 --> 00:05:37,301
[The visit was successful]
It was successful.

95
00:05:37,301 --> 00:05:39,874
I was very nervous coming here.

96
00:05:39,874 --> 00:05:41,457
Even though it was nerve-racking,

97
00:05:41,457 --> 00:05:45,735
it was worth coming all the way
to the factory here.

98
00:05:45,735 --> 00:05:51,048
It feels so rewarding, and I'm really excited.

99
00:05:51,048 --> 00:05:54,212
My profit isn't really my priority.

100
00:05:54,212 --> 00:05:56,620
I try to give the biggest discount possible.

101
00:05:56,620 --> 00:06:00,191
If the brand cannot offer a bigger discount
for the sake of fairness,

102
00:06:00,191 --> 00:06:04,601
I seek a way to reward the customers
with cashback points or extra benefits.

103
00:06:04,601 --> 00:06:06,263
I use all kinds of ways.

104
00:06:06,263 --> 00:06:09,733
I made up my mind when I joined X THE LEAGUE

105
00:06:09,733 --> 00:06:13,370
that I would learn as much as I can
and push my limits.

106
00:06:13,370 --> 00:06:16,879
I'd like to give it my all.

107
00:06:19,474 --> 00:06:22,812
[Fluke getting the Round 1 results]

108
00:06:22,812 --> 00:06:24,857
The gap is huge.

109
00:06:26,856 --> 00:06:29,286
[Thailand's shocking Round 1 ranking]

110
00:06:31,555 --> 00:06:33,224
Oh my god.

111
00:06:33,224 --> 00:06:34,624
No way.

112
00:06:37,794 --> 00:06:42,319
We need to find a solution.

113
00:06:42,319 --> 00:06:47,286
If this situation goes on, we can't survive.

114
00:06:47,791 --> 00:06:50,152
[Captain's Wild Card search begins]

115
00:06:50,152 --> 00:06:51,552
How about this person?

116
00:06:52,542 --> 00:06:55,109
I saw this one selling.

117
00:06:55,109 --> 00:06:56,313
Hello.

118
00:06:56,313 --> 00:06:58,582
How have you been?

119
00:06:58,582 --> 00:07:02,968
It's an international commerce competition.
Have you seen it?

120
00:07:02,968 --> 00:07:04,777
<i>I have. It's purple, right?</i>

121
00:07:04,777 --> 00:07:05,778
Right, right.

122
00:07:05,778 --> 00:07:07,878
This person gets a ton of viewers.

123
00:07:08,877 --> 00:07:10,299
Maybe I'll make a call.

124
00:07:10,299 --> 00:07:12,211
[Who will Captain Fluke choose?]

125
00:07:12,211 --> 00:07:13,439
In the first round,

126
00:07:13,439 --> 00:07:15,751
I realized just how strong the demand
for K-beauty products is.

127
00:07:15,751 --> 00:07:18,723
So I started looking
for K-beauty product sellers.

128
00:07:18,723 --> 00:07:23,386
That way, we will be able to make more sales.

129
00:07:24,485 --> 00:07:27,212
[Thai K-beauty queen, Tiffany]

130
00:07:27,807 --> 00:07:33,886
Tiffany is my strongest pick.

131
00:07:33,886 --> 00:07:35,403
[Cleansing products]

132
00:07:35,902 --> 00:07:37,832
[Makeup tools]

133
00:07:37,832 --> 00:07:40,638
[The beauty all-rounder who does it all]

134
00:07:41,212 --> 00:07:44,128
[Top-selling creator award winner]

135
00:07:44,128 --> 00:07:46,864
Hello, I'm Tiffany.

136
00:07:46,864 --> 00:07:49,500
I'm Team Thailand's Wild Card.

137
00:07:49,500 --> 00:07:53,103
Every TikTok user knows my nickname.

138
00:07:53,103 --> 00:07:54,703
The K-beauty queen.

139
00:07:55,499 --> 00:07:56,977
[No. 1 K-beauty trend leader]

140
00:07:56,977 --> 00:08:01,267
I'm based in Thailand.

141
00:08:01,267 --> 00:08:03,822
But I'm actively working
as a "K-beauty expert."

142
00:08:03,822 --> 00:08:10,642
[Tiffany frequently visits Korea
to stay on top of K-beauty trends]

143
00:08:10,642 --> 00:08:13,624
[Korea-related content dominates]

144
00:08:13,624 --> 00:08:17,197
I make content and meet a lot of brands.

145
00:08:17,197 --> 00:08:19,076
I also do livestreams.

146
00:08:19,661 --> 00:08:22,566
[A creator with a distinct identity]

147
00:08:22,566 --> 00:08:25,329
[What brings her to Korea today?]

148
00:08:25,329 --> 00:08:28,419
I'm at a beauty salon in Gangnam.

149
00:08:28,419 --> 00:08:32,476
I heard the makeup artist here
has worked with K-pop idols before.

150
00:08:32,476 --> 00:08:36,183
So today, I'm getting a makeover.

151
00:08:36,183 --> 00:08:39,116
[Tiffany visits a salon for an idol makeover]
Let's go.

152
00:08:39,116 --> 00:08:42,425
It was a great opportunity to see
what products makeup artists

153
00:08:42,425 --> 00:08:45,485
in the home of K-beauty actually use
to prep the skin.

154
00:08:48,492 --> 00:08:51,262
When I create content,

155
00:08:51,262 --> 00:08:53,502
we turn our plans into a script
and work from there.

156
00:08:53,502 --> 00:08:55,878
I strictly stick to the script.

157
00:08:55,878 --> 00:09:03,176
Viewers prefer videos that open
with a strong hook,

158
00:09:03,176 --> 00:09:05,591
that are easy to understand,
and that are not too long.

159
00:09:05,591 --> 00:09:08,412
[You must know the script inside and out]

160
00:09:08,412 --> 00:09:10,883
What kind of style would you like?

161
00:09:10,883 --> 00:09:11,974
IU.

162
00:09:11,974 --> 00:09:13,079
- IU?
- IU.

163
00:09:13,079 --> 00:09:14,964
- IU? Okay.
- Yes.

164
00:09:14,964 --> 00:09:17,658
Because I love Byeon Woo Seok.

165
00:09:17,658 --> 00:09:19,030
- Byeon Woo Seok?
- Yeah.

166
00:09:19,030 --> 00:09:22,588
Because they're shooting a TV series together.

167
00:09:22,588 --> 00:09:24,140
So I want to look like IU.

168
00:09:24,140 --> 00:09:25,892
- IU? Okay.
- Mmhmm.

169
00:09:25,892 --> 00:09:28,588
I saw Byeon Woo Seok yesterday,
so I came here today to look like IU.

170
00:09:28,588 --> 00:09:31,312
Will I be able to look like IU?

171
00:09:31,312 --> 00:09:33,373
[K-beauty fueling the Korean Wave]

172
00:09:33,373 --> 00:09:34,643
I'll start with skincare.

173
00:09:34,643 --> 00:09:37,741
[Starting with skincare]

174
00:09:37,741 --> 00:09:40,478
Should I ask the makeup artist
what skincare products she likes,

175
00:09:40,478 --> 00:09:43,047
or what products Koreans use?

176
00:09:43,047 --> 00:09:44,781
I have a question.

177
00:09:46,983 --> 00:09:49,483
- This is a really popular product.
- It is.

178
00:09:49,483 --> 00:09:51,355
- In Korea?
- Yes.

179
00:09:51,355 --> 00:09:54,466
[Why is she excited to see the product?]

180
00:09:54,466 --> 00:09:57,335
[It's a product Tiffany has featured before]

181
00:09:57,335 --> 00:10:00,963
[It's also her key product to sell]

182
00:10:00,963 --> 00:10:03,300
I was surprised.

183
00:10:03,300 --> 00:10:06,927
The makeup artist at the salon

184
00:10:06,927 --> 00:10:13,091
was using the product I'm selling.

185
00:10:13,091 --> 00:10:16,780
[Tiffany started livestreaming]

186
00:10:16,780 --> 00:10:21,109
I had a makeover in Korea today.

187
00:10:21,109 --> 00:10:22,920
They used this product as a base.

188
00:10:22,920 --> 00:10:25,456
[Makeup artist's pick]

189
00:10:25,456 --> 00:10:29,526
I asked her why she uses it
and what she likes about it.

190
00:10:29,526 --> 00:10:31,862
She said it's highly moisturizing
but still lightweight.

191
00:10:31,862 --> 00:10:34,876
[An expert's endorsement boosts
product credibility]

192
00:10:34,876 --> 00:10:38,597
If your skincare isn't properly prepped
before makeup,

193
00:10:38,597 --> 00:10:41,831
your makeup can cake up or slide off easily
because your skin is dry.

194
00:10:41,831 --> 00:10:45,001
[Tiffany highlighting the problem first]

195
00:10:45,001 --> 00:10:48,572
The way I do my livestreams is distinct
from how others do theirs.

196
00:10:48,572 --> 00:10:51,780
I start with the customer's pain points.

197
00:10:51,780 --> 00:10:55,685
[Pain point: an underlying concern consumers
have before realizing they need a product]

198
00:10:55,685 --> 00:10:57,563
If you have yellow teeth,
I'll give you 1,000 baht.

199
00:10:57,563 --> 00:11:00,272
- Can I see your teeth?
- Okay.

200
00:11:01,027 --> 00:11:03,595
Oh my god, why are my teeth so yellow?

201
00:11:03,595 --> 00:11:05,411
[Brushing her teeth]

202
00:11:05,411 --> 00:11:08,392
I show them the solution to their problem.

203
00:11:08,392 --> 00:11:11,975
[Her selling point is making people feel seen]

204
00:11:11,975 --> 00:11:15,750
I build up their emotions
and make them want to buy.

205
00:11:15,750 --> 00:11:18,538
[With storytelling
that sparks the desire to buy]

206
00:11:18,538 --> 00:11:27,062
[Tiffany sells K-beauty products]

207
00:11:27,062 --> 00:11:31,822
I promise my team I won't be a burden.

208
00:11:31,822 --> 00:11:35,883
I'll lead Team Thailand to the top.

209
00:11:36,823 --> 00:11:40,164
Third place is Singapore & Malaysia.

210
00:11:40,164 --> 00:11:45,035
When we checked the rankings,
we narrowly missed X1.

211
00:11:45,035 --> 00:11:47,271
The GMV gap was really small.

212
00:11:47,271 --> 00:11:49,740
If only we had done one more livestream,

213
00:11:49,740 --> 00:11:53,910
we could have at least overtaken the team
ahead of us.

214
00:11:53,910 --> 00:11:59,450
I want someone who can sell on
different platforms to join us.

215
00:11:59,450 --> 00:12:04,788
Then I want us to work together
to generate even higher GMV.

216
00:12:04,788 --> 00:12:07,727
When looking for the new Wild Card seller,

217
00:12:07,727 --> 00:12:12,615
what I was looking for was someone
who could broaden our reach across Malaysia.

218
00:12:12,615 --> 00:12:14,752
Because Malaysia is a big country,

219
00:12:14,752 --> 00:12:18,095
Elle and Sonia are based in Kuala Lumpur,
so our reach is limited.

220
00:12:18,095 --> 00:12:21,705
[A strategy to expand sales reach]

221
00:12:21,705 --> 00:12:25,278
I also considered
whether they could add real value to the team.

222
00:12:25,278 --> 00:12:30,612
I used my company data and platforms
to evaluate their credibility,

223
00:12:30,612 --> 00:12:33,281
check whether their fans are real,

224
00:12:33,281 --> 00:12:35,902
and how they engage with their fans.

225
00:12:35,902 --> 00:12:37,302
[Satisfied]

226
00:12:38,155 --> 00:12:40,056
I think I'll go with ***.

227
00:12:40,056 --> 00:12:42,878
This person's a perfect fit for Wild Card.

228
00:12:42,878 --> 00:12:46,486
[Wild Card to boost Team Singapore & Malaysia]

229
00:12:53,751 --> 00:12:56,107
[Jomama,
CEO with 9 billion won in monthly sales]

230
00:12:56,107 --> 00:12:57,622
Hi everyone, I'm Jomama.

231
00:12:57,622 --> 00:13:00,575
I'm from Johor Bahru, Malaysia.
I'm 45 years old this year.

232
00:13:00,575 --> 00:13:03,088
I'm a grandmother of two.

233
00:13:03,689 --> 00:13:05,278
Baby.

234
00:13:05,278 --> 00:13:08,786
Baby. Hello.

235
00:13:08,786 --> 00:13:11,288
I have a lovely mom.

236
00:13:11,288 --> 00:13:14,458
I have two sons and a daughter.

237
00:13:14,458 --> 00:13:18,153
My eldest is 24 this year,
and he's already married.

238
00:13:18,153 --> 00:13:20,503
I have two grandchildren.

239
00:13:21,031 --> 00:13:23,901
There are seven in total,
and eight including me.

240
00:13:23,901 --> 00:13:26,823
[Four generations of one big family]
In Chinese culture, it's very good.

241
00:13:27,576 --> 00:13:32,017
I'm the Wild Card
for Team Singapore & Malaysia.

242
00:13:33,310 --> 00:13:36,013
I'm the founder of Jomama Online Shop.

243
00:13:37,912 --> 00:13:41,752
Jomama Online Shop kicked off
five to six years ago.

244
00:13:41,752 --> 00:13:44,460
[An online store specializing
in beauty, home, and lifestyle products]

245
00:13:44,460 --> 00:13:47,735
We had a very good record last year.

246
00:13:47,735 --> 00:13:51,720
We made 30 million ringgit in a year.
Just my personal sales.

247
00:13:52,793 --> 00:13:55,961
We made it into the Malaysia Book of Records
last year.

248
00:13:56,467 --> 00:14:02,671
